<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iller</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Iller is a river that rises near Oberstdorf in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allgau">Allgäu</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> and flows north through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kempten">Kempten</a> to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> at Ulm. For much of its course it forms the border between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>. Kempten grew at a crossing on its banks in Roman times as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodunum">Cambodunum</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iller.jpg" alt="Iller" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: cinecol · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illertal-2008-12-29b.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
